# Migrating an existing project to the delivery system

This template version adds the delivery system: a tracked `working/` directory,
new Makefile targets, checks in CI, session hooks for Claude Code, and a new
`AGENTS.md`. Projects generated from an earlier version can adopt it with
`copier update --trust --skip-answered` followed by:

    bash scripts/migrate-to-delivery.sh --from <a freshly generated project>

`--from` is required: the script copies the new directories out of a project
generated from this template version, so it needs one to copy from. Generate a
throwaway one next to your project and point at it.

The script:

1. creates `working/` with the standards, templates, and an empty constraints
   file (nothing is overwritten if it exists);
2. reports which replaced files you had modified locally (`Makefile`,
   `.github/workflows/ci.yml`, `AGENTS.md`,
   `.github/pull_request_template.md`, `.pre-commit-config.yaml`) so you can
   merge your changes by hand;
3. restores `docs/` from the template.

`copier update` also brings in `pyproject.toml` changes (Ruff rules,
import-linter, the `spec` pytest marker, dev dependencies); review that diff.

`docs/` stays untracked, as before. `.gitignore` is unchanged.

After migrating: `make hooks`, register your SSH key as a GitHub signing key
(see `working/README.md#signing`), enable the process per member by adding
`[tool.delivery] enabled = true` to that member's `pyproject.toml`, and write
the member's living spec under `working/spec/<name>.md`. A member without one
is reported as unspecified and is not blocked.
